1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Diego de Montoya, II''' born c. 1658 at died 1717, age 59
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Josefa-de-Hinojos/6000000005599001861 Maria Josefa de Hinojos]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Diego de Montoya, II and Maria Josefa de Hinojos:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Montoya/6000000000401594355?through=6000000007528901004 Maria de la Rosa Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juan-Montoya/6000000007529122154?through=6000000007529145667 Juan Esteban Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Lucia-de-Montoya/6000000007529153247?through=6000000007528901004 Lucia Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Antonio-Montoya/6000000007528901004?through=6000000007529122154 Antonio Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Salvador-Montoya/6000000007529145667 Salvador Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juana-Montoya/6000000005599075537 Juana Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Miguel-Montoya/6000000000401594378?through=6000000005599075537 Miguel de la Cruz Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Montoya/6000000007529143039?through=6000000000401594378 Maria Isabel Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Marcial-Montoya/6000000007529142371?through=6000000007529143039 Marcial Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Francisca-Montoya/6000000000401594371?through=6000000007529142371 Maria Francisca Montoya]
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego de Montoya, II is the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Diego-de-Montoya-I/6000000005599075590?through=6000000005599075599 Diego de Montoya, I] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Ortiz-de-Vera/6000000005599209693?through
2 CONC =6000000005599075599 Maria Ortiz de Vera]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT He appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth household, three sons, three daughters, two servants
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Diego Montoya''', regidor, married to Josefa de Hinojos, with six children: Salvador, three; Juan Estevan, five; Antonio, three; Maria de la Rosa, eight; Luisa, four; Juana, two.  Likewise, this household has two married servan
2 CONC ts named Antonio and his wife, Ana Duran.  He states that, as a loyal vassal of his majesty, he is quite ready to enter to settle with his wife and children when I, the governor and captain general, enter.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Spanish Archives of New Mexico, he is listed as a chief alcalde and member of the cabildo of Santa Fe, in 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/110326636/person/120127046630 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 22 2017, 18:17:50 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/110326636/person/120127046630 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 3 2017, 13:10:22 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego de Montoya became part of the assembly in 1680 with his wife and two children. He was twenty-three years old in 1681, described as a new Mexican, married or of good stature, with wide shoulders, good features, thick beard an
2 CONC d long, straight hair. He was Antonio de Montoya's brother. His wife was María de Hinajosa, and they returned to New Mexico with Don Diego de Vargas in 1693.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego Montoya went to live in the city of Santa Fe, occupied by the Indians, as soon as the settlers arrived there in 1693, but was warned of the imminent rebellion, so he camped outside the city walls with the rest of the settler
2 CONC s. A few years later he moved to Bernalillo with other former inhabitants who preferred the Río Abajo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego's wife was Josefa de Hinojos, they had at least five children. These children were: Salvador, married to Manuela García de la Riva; Juana, first wife of Pedro Durán y Cháves; Isabel, wife of Miguel de San Juan; and one more 
2 CONC daughter who was the second wife of Baltasar Romero.
2 CONT
2 CONT Census: Meeting of the El Paso Area of Don Diego de Vargas, Dec 1692-Ene 1693, Guadalupe del Paso, New Mexico. New Spain. 287
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth home, three sons, three daughters, two servants
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego Montoya, councillor, married to Josefa de Hinojos, with six children: Salvador, three; Juan Estaban, five; Antonio, three; María de la Rosa, eight; Luisa, four; Juana, two. Likewise, this home has married servants named Anti
2 CONC onio and his wife, Ana Durán.
