1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Died during the Pueblo Revolt of 1680.  Her two daughters escaped the massacre of 1680; possibly they were captured by the Taos Indians and were rescued in 1692, or else they were with their mother's relatives who 
2 CONC escaped. One of these was María who became the wife of Sebastián Martín Serrano, and the other was Josefa who married Antonio de Cisneros.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Fray Angelico Chavez, Origins of New Mexico Families, Revised Edition 1992, 22.
