2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Lucero de Godoy is the son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Juan-Lucero-De-Godoy/6000000008212796914?through=6000000005598867328 Juan Antonio Lucero De Godoy, I] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Juana-de-Carvajal/600000000150
2 CONC 0813866?through=6000000008212796914 Juana de Carvajal]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT He appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Third household, three sons, two daughters, two sisters, one orphan girl
2 CONT
2 CONT Adjutant '''Antonio Lucero''', regidor, married to Maria Antonia Varela de Perea, with three sons and two daughters: Antonio, five; Juan, three; Diego, one; Martina, fifteen; Bernardina, seven; two sisters, the one a widow named G
2 CONC eronima, without children, and the other, Maria, eighteen; and an orphan girl, eleven.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Came back to New Mexico with his second wife, Antonia Varela.  Early in the century he was asking for Santa Fe lands that had belonged to his father, Juan.  He belonged to La Conquisadora Confraternity.
