2 ADDR
3 CITY San Juan Pueblo Nuevo Mexico
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Note:''' Maria was the daughter of  Fernando Duran y Chávez, II and she was adopted by her stepfather, Miguel Luján, who married her mother, Elena Ruiz Caceras.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maria Duran y Chávez de Lujan''' born 1673 at Nuevo México, Nueva España, died after May 2, 1765 at Nuesto de Nuestra Sra de la Soledad, Nuevo México, Nueva España 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Ben M. Angel notes: This is the Puesta de Nuestra Señora de la Soledad del Rio del Norte Arriba, or present Hacienda de los Luceros - http://books.google.by/books?id=SSXRGB21WH4C&pg=PA43&lpg=PA43&dq=Nuestra+Senora+de+la+Soledad+d
2 CONC el+Rio+del+Norte&source=bl&ots=inMfFfI8hI&sig=gfUMD_SFs8MfxJQdUTJ1s4ktvqE&hl=ru&sa=X&ei=7TQeUa6yIsbitQbD0IE4&sqi=2&ved=0CEcQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=Nuestra%20Senora%20de%20la%20Soledad%20del%20Rio%20del%20Norte&f=false )
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother died during the Pueblo Revolt of 1680.  Maria and her sister escaped the massacre of 1680; possibly they were captured by the Taos Indians and were rescued in 1692, or else they were with their mother's relatives who es
2 CONC caped. María became the wife of Sebastián Martín Serrano, and the other was Josefa who married Antonio de Cisneros.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1765, she signed her last will and testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Fray Angelico Chavez, Origins of New Mexico Families, Revised Edition 1992, 22.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694. John L. Kessell, Rick Hendricks, a Meredith Dodge, Editors.
