1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The New Mexican of Wednesday, June 6, 1973:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://searchapi.newspaperarchive.com/cache/50533290.pdf?forcedownload
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez:
2 CONT
2 CONT MARIANO ROYBAL and Maria Loreta Velasquez were married at La Cuchilla on June 27, 1781. His wife's surname is omitted in the marriage entry, and in the baptisms of some children, while in others it appears several times as Ortiz, 
2 CONC then as Velarde or Valverde, but most often as Velasquez, the name of the family which had reared her. Maria Loreta Ortiz, widow of Mariano Roybal, died on May 26, 1845, leaving seven surviving children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of their very large family, the sons are as follows:
2 CONT *1. Juan de Dios, born May 9, 1789: 
2 CONT *2. Juan Manuel, January 16, 1787, who married Maria Josefa Quintana;
2 CONT *3. Rafael Vicente, August 7, 1791, who married Anastasia Quintana; 
2 CONT *4. Jose Juan, February 16, 1798, who married Maria Juliana Quintana, and
2 CONT *5. Jose de Jesus, June 1, 1800, who married Margarita Duran.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known daughters were:
2 CONT *1. Maria Manuela, May 21, 1783;
2 CONT *2. Teodora, April 1, 1785, who married Pedro Martin, April 14, 1804, 
2 CONT *3. Juana Barbara, April 23, 1973; and 
2 CONT *4. Maria Antonia, October 25, 1795, who married Pedro Gonzalez.
