1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1790
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From descendant Jose Antonio Esquibel (noted New Mexico family historian):
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.goodreads.com/author/show/1060505.Jose_Antonio_Esquibel/blog/tag/buenaventura-esquibel
2 CONT
2 CONT My direct paternal ancestor, Juan Esquibel, was a resident of theVilla de Santa Fe living in the household of María Francisca Esquibel in 1750. Based on a variety of supporting documentation, he may have been one of the eight chil
2 CONC dren of Buenaventura de Esquibel and Rosa Bernardina Lucero de Godoy, or perhaps he was a grandson. He was identified as 'español' (Spanish) and a soldier when he was married at Ojo Caliente, New Mexico, on October 5, 1758, with F
2 CONC eliciana Durán, born December 1741, Ojo Caliente, NM, a daughter Francisco Durán and Isabel Martín.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Esquibel and María Francisca Esquibel (most likley his sister, or even perhaps his mother) were godparents for a child of José Esquibel Araus and Juana Manuel López baptized in the church of Santa Cruz de la Cañada on January
2 CONC  29, 1748. Juan Esquibel and María Francisca Esquibel were godparents for a daughter of María Rita Esquibel and Juan de Beita (Abeyta) baptized on December 9, 1755, in the church of San Francisco in Santa Fe. Juan Esquibel gave th
2 CONC e name of Buenaventura to one of his sons, another indication of a familial connection with Buenaventura de Esquibel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan Esquibel and his wife Feliciana Durán christened their first son as Buenaventura, apparently in honor of the child's paternal grandfather, a common custom among Spanish families (or is it the child maternal great-grandfather?
2 CONC ). By the mid-1780's Juan Esquibel and his family were residents of the jurisdiction of San Juan Pueblo, having settled at the village of La Canoa, north of the pueblo and along the Rio Grande.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Hispanic Genealogical Research Center of New Mexico's Great New Mexico Pedigree Database:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hgrc-nm.org/surnames/GNMPD.html/d0043/g0004331.html#I19243
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan ESQUIBEL [13959] [13960]
2 CONT *ABT 1740 - ____
2 CONT *BIRTH: ABT 1740
2 CONT *DEATH: Y
2 CONT *Father: Buenaventura Miguel ESQUIBEL (based on present information, approx. age 56 at birth)
2 CONT *Mother: Rosa Bernadina LUCERO DE GODOY (based on presented information, approx. age 54 at birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 : Feliciana DURAN (b. 1738, parents born around 1710)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. +Buenaventura ESQUIBEL (b. 1759, m. Ana Teresa Romero, b. 1765)
2 CONT **2. +Maria Rosalia ESQUIBEL (m. Jose Baltasar Lobato, b. 1766)
2 CONT **3. +Maria de la Luz ESQUIBEL (m. Antonio Jose Martin, b. 1762)
2 CONT **4. +Maria Encarnacion ESQUIBEL (m. Jose Miguel Antonio Vigil, b. 1758)
2 CONT **5. +Juaquin Rafael ESQUIBEL (m. Maria Barbara Pino, children born 1795-1798, and Maria Candelaria, children born 1817-1832)
2 CONT **6. +Jose Cipriano ESQUIBEL  (b. c1780, m. Casilda Cordova, child born 1802, and in 1803 Barbara Rafaela Quintana, children born 1804-1815)
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes:
2 CONT *[13959] [S13] New Mexico Genealogist--NMGS, June 1992, p. 50-58
2 CONT *[13960] [S13] New Mexico Genealogist--NMGS, June 1992, p. 50-58
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: His mother's age is unusual, if born in 1740. It is likely that he was born much earlier (his next nearest sibling was born in 1720). But will retain c1740 until a better source is provided.
