1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miguel_Hidalgo '''Miguel Hidalgo y Costilla'''], was a Mexican Roman Catholic priest and a leader of the Mexican War of Independence.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a professor at the Colegio de San Nicolás Obispo in Valladolid and was ousted in 1792. He served in a church in Colima and then in Dolores, Dias. After his arrival, he was shocked by the rich soil he had found. He tried to 
2 CONC help the poor by showing them how to grow olives and grapes, but in Mexico, growing these crops was discouraged or prohibited by the authorities due to Spanish imports of the items. In 1810 he gave the famous speech, "The Cry of D
2 CONC olores", calling upon the people to protect the interest of their King [https://www.geni.com/people/Fernando-VII-El-Deseado-King-of-Spain/6000000003231189183 Fernando VII] (held captive by Napoleon) by revolting against the Europe
2 CONC an-born Spaniards who had overthrown the Spanish Viceroy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He marched across Mexico and gathered an army of nearly 90,000 poor farmers and Mexican civilians who attacked and killed both Spanish Peninsulares and Criollo elites, even though Hidalgo's troops lacked training and were poorly a
2 CONC rmed. These troops ran into an army of 6,000 well-trained and armed Spanish troops; most of Hidalgo's troops fled or were killed at the Battle of Calderón Bridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/259911316/miguel-hidalgo_y_costilla
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides being a revolutionary, Hidalgo was also a philosopher, see https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/philosophy-mexico/: "Several Mexican thinkers appealed to scholastic political philosophy to answer affirmatively to the questio
2 CONC n, and also—though not always explicitly— to the philosophy of the Enlightenment. Such was the case of Miguel Hidalgo (1753–1811), father of Mexican Independence. Hidalgo’s predilection for French ideas was well known, but he was 
2 CONC also known for his opposition to Aristotelian-based scholastic theology displayed in his Disertación sobre el verdadero método de estudiar teología escolástica (1784)."
