1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Vallejos, a 26 year old Mulatto man, and his wife Rosalia Garcia, a 20 year old Mulatta woman, were living in Alburquerque in 1750. Their children who were living with them at the time were Juan Miguel, 3 ye
2 CONC ars old and Maria Barbara, 1 year old. Antonia Garcia, a single 22 year old Mulatta woman, was also living there with her 7 year old son Juan Pedro. An eight year old Indian girl by the name of Magdalena also lived in the househol
2 CONC d. [Olmsted. Spanish and Mexican Censuses of New Mexico: 1750-1840. Pg. 87.]
