1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antonio Félix Sedillo was born about 1740 and married Antonia Narcisa Baca 1 July 1770 at Mission San José, Pueblo of Laguna.  In the 1790 census of Albuquerque, Antonio Sedillo, Antonia Baca and their children wer
2 CONC e enumerated as residents of Plaza number 4 of Atrisco in household number 278.  Antonia Narcisa Baca was born about 1757.  They had 8 children:  José Manuel, Antonio Toribio, Andres Antonio, Juan Blas, Julian Bernardo, Andres Gre
2 CONC gorio, (Julian and Andres were twins), Maria Guadalupe de los Delores (died as a child - about 6 or 7 years old) and José Blas Sedillo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Title: Origins of New Mexico Families, Revised Edition 1992 Author: Fray Angelico Chavez Publication: Revised Edition, 1982; Museum of NM Press. Repository:  Media: Book Page: 145 Title: New Mexico Colonial Censuses: 1790
2 CONC , 1823, 1845 Author: transcribed and compiled by Virginia Langham Olmstead, GRS Publication: NMGS, Inc., Note: Spanish & Mexican Colonial Censuses Repository:  Media: Book Page: 16 Text: 16-1790, Alburquerqque, Plaza #4 of Atrisco
2 CONC ; #278: Antonio Sedillo, S,42, farmer, m. Maria Antonia Baca; S, 33; 6 sons; and servants/others
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of this information is from 'Aqui Se Comienza' - A Genealogical History of the Founding Families of La Villa de San Felipe De Albuquerque.
