1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alburquerque. July 10, 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartolo Gallego was wounded in his home in Ysleta. He awakes thinking he was attacked by Apaches. General alarm sounded but no signs of them. Ramos Sedillo was seen armed some time before. Arrested and confessed to having planned 
2 CONC to murder Gallego. Claimed Gallego's wife was in on it and that they planned to marry afterwards. Maria Dolores Saez (wife) denies this. Diligencias are sent to the governor.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://uair.arizona.edu/item/221918
