1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Thursday, June 18, 2015, blog entry of Eddie Romero:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://enjoythetimeleft.blogspot.com/2015/06/?m=0
2 CONT
2 CONT (In) the book “The Descendents of Lucero de Godoy” by Margaret Buxton... the family I was researching was Marcos Lucero de Godoy and his wife Maria Antonia Gomez del Castillo. This family had a daughter named Maria Andrea Lucero m
2 CONC arried to a Juan Domingo Valdes. On pages 89 and 172 Margaret Buxton indicates that Juan Domingo Valdes and Maria Andrea Lucero had a daughter named Maria Paula Valdes married to a Manuel Ricardo Romero. Was this a coincidence? Ma
2 CONC rriage information listed indicated a marriage in 1792 in San Ildefonso.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Juan de Jesus was a known son of Juan Domingo Valdes and Andrea Lucero as indicated on page 137 in the book “The Spanish Re-colonization of New Mexico” by Jose Esquibel and John Colligan. Generally, the tradition is that the gr
2 CONC andparents would baptize one child and then some of the brothers and/or sisters might be padrinos for another child.
