1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "Baptisms, Alari, Alarid, Alire Surnames, Santa Fe County, New Mexico" submitted by Yolanda R. Chavez, on 26 Sep 2017
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/nm/santafe/church/alari-bapt.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT ALARI, ALARID AND ALIRE SURNAME SANTA FE COUNTY, NM
2 CONT
2 CONT ALBUQUERQUE MAIN LIBRARY FILM
2 CONT *SANTA FE Baptisms Reels 15, 16 & 17 Films 0016893, 0016894 & 0016895
2 CONT *SANTA FE Marriages Reels 31 & 89 Films 0016899 & 0016900
2 CONT *Spanish Archives of New Mexico - UNM Zimmerman Library
2 CONT *Military Census - Virginia L. Olmstead, New Mexico Genealogical Society
2 CONT *Military Census 1890 - familysearch.org
2 CONT *Pre Nup Investigations - Fray Angelico Chavez, unmrepository.unm.edu
2 CONT
2 CONT ALARI, Manuel Ysidro (M)
2 CONT *Baptism     6 Apr 1751 in Santa Fe, NM
2 CONT *Military    Married farmer of Santa Fe. 5'5" age 28. Black hair and eyebrows, dark eyes, fair rosy skin, straight nose, heavy beard, scars on right eye tear duct and back of neck. Signed 11 Jan 1816, signed by mark, service recor
2 CONC d. Died 13 April 1804, Santa Fe.
2 CONT *Birth       Santa Fe, NM
2 CONT *Parents     Juan Bautista D'ALARIE and Maria Francisca FERNANDEZ DE LA PEDRERA
2 CONT *Spouse      Maria Juana Josefa de ARMENTA
2 CONT *Marriage    20 Feb 1772 in Santa Fe, NM
2 CONT *Spouse      Maria Josefa de Jesus ORTIZ
2 CONT *Marriage    21 Dec 1781 in Santa Fe, NM
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT 1a, 1c. enl 11 Jan 1779, Sonora 1780/81, 21:832, farmer, son of Juan Bautista de Alaríd and María Francisca Fernández de la Pedrera of SF. 1d. PSF, en cavallada in 1785. 2a, wife listed as: Josefa Ortíz. He md (1) María Josefa de 
2 CONC Armenta on 20 Feb 1772 at SF, but she died 9 Mar 1781 at La Castrense. Their ch were José de Jesús, bap 23 Nov 1773, SF; and María Rita de Jesús, bap 29 May 1776, SF. He md (2) on 21 Dec 1781 at La Castrense, SF, Josefa Ortiz Bust
2 CONC amante: children; Joaquin, md María Luz Chávez of Tomé; José María, md María Guadalupe Rivera 20 Apr 1814, SF; José Manuel (1804 - ), md Isabel Urioste; Mariano José (1802 - ), md María Luz Martínez; and Ana María, md Vicente Vill
2 CONC anueva.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuel Ysidro's military record states that he was a farmer, married, and aged 28 when he joined the military on January 11, 1779. He signed his name with a mark which indicates he may have been illiterate. He is described as havi
2 CONC ng black hair and eyebrows, fair rosy skin, a straight nose, heavy beard, and scars on his right eye tear duct and back of his neck. He was still enlisted when he died on April 13, 1804 in Santa Fe.
1 NOTE {geni:hair_color} Black
1 NOTE {geni:eye_color} Brown
1 NOTE {geni:height_1} 5 feet
1 NOTE {geni:height_2} 5 inches
