3 CITY Valencia
3 STAE NM
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU RancherTrader/Judge/Politician
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information provided by Joseph H. Sanchez, 3rd great grandson
2 CONT
2 CONT Who at the ripe old age of seventy years, stands today as one of New Mexico's prominent influential and energetic men, born September 16, 1817 in the little old town of Valencia, New Mexico. He had but a limited educational advant
2 CONC ages. During the years 1838-39, he did considerable trade with Old Mexico for both himself and his father. In 1840 he married to Miss Juana Maria Chavez; ten children have blessed the union, seven of whom are now living. In 1849 M
2 CONC r Chavez was elected clerk of the probate court and held that office for ten years. In 1852 he was elected justice of the peace for Valencia County. He held the position of Representative in the New Mexico Legislature in 1863. Dur
2 CONC ing the years 1867-68 he was United States deputy internal revenue collector. Several times he was appointed quartermaster for the entire New Mexico Militia. In 1862 he was stationed at Fort Craig, New Mexico, and at this point he
2 CONC  formed an auxiliary company which did good service. He has many friends and is an honored and respected citizen .
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "New Mexico, The Spanish Conquest to the Present Time" by Helen Hines, printed 1881-sub by Pat Hines.  Note: Profile and photo were taken from this book.
