1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jose Antonio and his brother Dionicio moved to Socorro around the 1820's they owned a store. They were friends to some Apaches. One day an Apache came to warn them that they were going to attack the village of Soco
2 CONC rro at dawn and told them to stay out of sight. Naturally the two brothers spread the alarm , the people were not caught by surprise. The Apaches retreated toward the hills pursued by two groups, one on horseback and the other on 
2 CONC foot. Due to a mistake in signals the two groups got farther apart than they planned. The Apaches attacked on the group on foot and killed everyone including Jose Antonio and Dionicio 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jose Antonio and his brother Dionicio moved to Socorro around the 1820's they owned a store. They were friends to some Apaches. One day an Apache came to warn them that they were going to attack the village of Socorro at dawn and 
2 CONC told them to stay out of sight. Naturally the two brothers spread the alarm , the people were not caught by surprise. The Apaches retreated toward the hills pursued by two groups, one on horseback and the other on foot. Due to a m
2 CONC istake in signals the two groups got farther apart than they planned. The Apaches attacked on the group on foot and killed everyone including Jose Antonio and Dionicio 
