1 NAME José Ramón /Alari/
2 GIVN José Ramón
2 SURN Alari
2 _MARNM Alari
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE AFT 1783
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fe
3 STAE Provincia de Nuevo México
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1841
2 ADDR
3 CITY Probably San Miguel del Vado
3 STAE Nuevo México
3 CTRY Mexico
1 OCCU Farmer and Alcalde
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jose Ramon Alari enlisted in the military on March 20, 1802 at the age of 19, and was discharged from the military due to chronic illness in 1816. He was listed as a farmer at the time of his enlistment. During his
2 CONC  time in the military, he served in six military campaigns.  In his enlistment record he is described as being 5'1, with chestnut hair and eyebrows, black eyes, fair skin, straight nose,  a thin beard, and a mole on his right chec
2 CONC k. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *When he married his second wife, Manuela Antonia Jaramillo, he adopted her illegitimate son, Ramon Antonio (nickname Romancito). 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1824, Jose Ramon Alari and his second wife, Manuela were living in the Pecos Valley, when he and 14 other men were awarded a land grant in what is today, El Cerrito, NM. From 1826 until his death in 1841, he served as Alcalde o
2 CONC f El Cerrito, and was instrumental in fortifying the town from attacks from nearby tribes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *El Cerrito, New Mexico: Eight Generations in a Spanish Village
