2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT There was an Ignacio Roibal/Ygnacio Roybal who served in Company A, First Regiment, New Mexico Infantry (Union) during the American Civil War (entered as a private, exited as a corporal), but there is nothing that confirms this to
2 CONC  be the same person. Being age 32 at the time of the war, it is a likely match, though.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unit History from the National Parks Service:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nps.gov/civilwar/search-regiments-detail.htm?regiment_id=UNM0001RI02
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Regiment, New Mexico Infantry (New)
2 CONT
2 CONT OVERVIEW: 
2 CONT *Organized at October 1, 1863. 
2 CONT *Attached to Department of New Mexico and on garrison duty by detachments at Forts Union, Solden, Craig, Bowie, Cummings, McRae, Goodwin and other points in that Department during entire term of service. 
2 CONT *Expedition to Pinal Creek August 1-5, 1864. 
2 CONT *Expedition from Fort Craig to Fort Goodwin, Ariz., October 1-November 27, 1864. 
2 CONT *Mustered out November 7, 1866.
