1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The New Mexican of Wednesday, June 6, 1973:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://searchapi.newspaperarchive.com/cache/50533290.pdf?forcedownload
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico Chavez:
2 CONT
2 CONT Desiderio Roybal, son of Juan Manuel Roybal and Maria Josefa Quintana, married Maria Dolores Alarid of Santa Fe at El Rancho, February 16, 1846. According to their children's baptisms and marriages, they were living at Buena Vista
2 CONC  east of Mora in 1853, at La Cebolla in 1861-1867, and at Los Fuertecitos by 1885.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known children were:
2 CONT *1. Romualdo Abad, born at Jacona on April 6, 1849, who married Maria Monica Gonzalez; 
2 CONT *2. Jose Teodoro, April 1, 1851, who married Juana Valdes in 1876, and then Eugenia Velasquez at La Cebolla, January 26, 1885; 
2 CONT *3. Jose Ignacio, born at Buena Vista, August 1, 1853, 
2 CONT *4. Maria Albina, November 27, 1854, who married Jose Maria Martin, November 11, 1867; 
2 CONT *5. Maria Trinidad born at Jacona, February 4, 1847, 
2 CONT *6. the infants, Maria Rita and 
2 CONT *7. Francisco, buried at La Cueva in 1861 and 1864, and
2 CONT *8.  Fructuosa, who married Sacramento Baca, Feburary 10, 1879.
