2 SURN Casias
2 _MARNM Valdez
2 NICK José de los Reyes
2 NICK Chaves
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
1 BIRT
2 DATE MAY 1853
2 ADDR
3 CITY Probably La Culebra
3 STAE New Mexico Territory
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Bookkeeper for his step father, farmer, likely at least half Indian
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth place not confirmed:
2 CONT
2 CONT Suggestion of San Luis de Culebra, Taos County, New Mexico Territory (presently San Luis in Colorado) is based on an entry on Page 311 in the 1860 Census of the Precinct of Culebra, Taos County, Territory of New Mexico, conducted 
2 CONC by Pedro Valdez on July 17, 1860, which identified in residence 1881 an infant named Reyes Casillas: 
2 CONT * Jose Casillos, age 35 (born 1825), male, teamster, born in Taos County, (80 US dollars in personal estate, cannot read or write in English)
2 CONT *Esqupula Maes, age 30 (born 1830), female, born in Rio Arriba County (cannot read or write in English)
2 CONT *Donaciana Casillos, age 7 (born 1853), female, born in Taos County
2 CONT *Jose Maria Casillos, age 4 (born 1856), male, born in Taos County
2 CONT *Reyes Casillos, age 6 months (born January 1860), male, born in Taos County
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:33SQ-GBSZ-TMN?i=9&cc=1473181
2 CONT
2 CONT This Reyes Casillos was baptized as Jose de los Reyes Casias at the Nuestra Senora de los Dolores Church in Arroyo Hondo on Jan. 10, 1860. It might be possible that this Reyes was born to an Ascension Casias, who was listed as bei
2 CONC ng 14 years old in the 1860 Census, enumerated by Pedro Valdez on Aug. 21, 1860 at the Pueblo of Taos (who lived in the household of Rafael Reina, age 25, and Ascension's sister Dolores Casias, age 15, daughter of Benito Casias an
2 CONC d Francisca Romero, as well as Santiago Casias, age 5, and Juana Casias, age 3):
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:33SQ-GBSZ-52B?i=2&cc=1473181
2 CONT
2 CONT ... but because the record indicates that he was the son of Jose Casias and Escipula Maes, it's difficult to prove that this is the same Reyes Casias who later married Albina Romero, said to be born in 1854 according to the 1880 c
2 CONC ensus, and in May 1853 according to the 1900 census.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Reyes Casias, mentioned in the record of Reyes Casias and Maria Albina Romero
2 CONT
2 CONT *Name	Reyes Casias
2 CONT *Spouse's Name	Maria Albina Romero
2 CONT *Event Date	28 Nov 1874
2 CONT *Event Place	San Juan De Los Caballeros-Catholic, San Juan, Rio Arriba, New Mexico
2 CONT *Mother's Name	Maria Asension Casias
2 CONT *Spouse's Father's Name	Maria De La Cruz Romero
2 CONT
2 CONT "New Mexico Marriages, 1751-1918," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FDPV-R21 : accessed 22 May 2016), Reyes Casias and Maria Albina Romero, 28 Nov 1874; citing San Juan De Los Caballeros-Catholic, Sa
2 CONC n Juan, Rio Arriba, New Mexico, reference 2:26WJ0X8; FHL microfilm 16,979.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
