2 CONT
2 CONT * 	Household	Gender	Age	Birthplace
2 CONT *head	 Reyes Valdez	M	44	 New Mexico (est. b. 1856, actually b. 1859)
2 CONT *wife	Alvina Valdez	F	35	 New Mexico (est. b. 1865)
2 CONT *son	Elias Valdez	M	20	 New Mexico (est. b. 1880, actually born 1881)
2 CONT *daughter	Emiliana Valdez	F	9	 New Mexico (est. b. 1891, actually Cipriana, b. 1891)
2 CONT *daughter	Celestina Valdez	F	7	 New Mexico (est. b. 1893, actually b. 1894)
2 CONT
2 CONT "United States Census, 1900," index and images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/MMLS-J4F : accessed 10 Feb 2013), Reyes Valdez, ED 81 Precincts 1, 25 Embudo, La Jolla, Rio Arriba, New Mexico Territory, United S
2 CONC tates; citing sheet 2B, family 44, NARA microfilm publication T623, FHL microfilm 1241001.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albina's birth date estimates vary widely. In the 1900 census, it was estimated that the two were married in 1877, but that Albina was only 12 at the time of marriage. This varies greatly from her self-disclosed age in 1880, when 
2 CONC she said she was 24, or about 21 at the time of her marriage. Birth records, however, show her to have given birth to their first child, Rakel, in 1876. Unlike Reyes and Albina's second child, Ramon, she apparently didn't survive 
2 CONC to the 1880 census as she did not appear there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
