0 @N6000000005024488509@ NOTE Catholic
1 CONT AKA: PEDRO PéREZ DE ZAMORA.
1 CONT ______________________________
1 CONT ZAMORA (MONTOYA) -Promising Lead
1 CONT
1 CONT María de Zamora (ONMF: 77), wife of Bartolomé de Montoya, was identified by Chávez as being a daughter of Pedro de Zamora and Agustina de Abarca. Chávez's source indicates that Pedro de Zamora was a former Alcalde Mayor of Oaxaca 
1 CONC before coming to reside at Mexico City in the neighborhood of San Sebastián. Among the prominent citizens of Oaxaca in the sixteenth century were members of the Pérez de Zamora family. Members of this family went by these intercha
1 CONC ngable surnames: Zamora, Pérez, Pérez de Zamora, and González. 
1 CONT
1 CONT In the latter part of the 1500s there was a Pedro Pérez de Zamora of Oaxaca who was described as being "en corregimiento," which indicates he was somehow involved as a city official. His uncle Luis de Zamora (aka Luis Pérez de Zam
1 CONC ora held various alcaldías mayores for as many as thirty years in the latter half of the 1500s.
1 CONT
1 CONT Pedro Pérez de Zamora was married at Oaxaca and was a son of Alvaro de Zamora (aka Alvaro Pérez de Zamora). Alvaro Pérez de Zamora was a son of Alonso Pérez de Zamora, a conquistador de México. Alvaro's wife was doña Catalina de O
1 CONC campo, the third child of don Sebastián de Saavedra and doña Catalina de Ocampo. (Sebastián de Saavedra was a native of Sevilla, and a son of Sebastián de Saavedra and doña Isabel de Sanabria, native of Carmona -belonging to the S
1 CONC anabria and Sotomayor familes of this town).
1 CONT
1 CONT Batltasar Dorantes de Carranza recorded the following infmation about the Zamora family: "Alonso Pérez de Zamora y Alvaro Pérez, padre y hijo, fueron de los primeros conquistadores de esta Nueva España; dejo muchos hijos e hijas p
1 CONC obres, y estan despseidos de pueblos, que son los peñoles de Oaxaca y otros que le dieron en la Provincia de Guatemala".
1 CONT
1 CONT Was Pedro de Zamora (identified as Alcalde Mayor de Oaxaca and father of María de Zamora) related to the Pérez de Zamora clan? Was this Pedro de Zamora the same person as Pedro Pérez de Zamora? Further research into the genealogy 
1 CONC of the Pérez de Zamora family, and into the records from sixteenth century Oaxaca may help to answer this question one way or the other.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dorantes de Carranza added this additional information in his account of people of Nueva España that may prove useful in any further Zamora family research: "Alvaro de Zamora dejo un hijo y dos hijas; el hijo [Pedro Pérez de Zamor
1 CONC a] casó en Oaxaca; tiene en la real caja 130 pesos y 200 fanegas de maíz en el pueblo de Tepozotlan. De esta caas proveen a Pedro Pérez de Zamora, en corregimiento, y a Luis de Vargas, su cuñado, en corregimiento, por hermano. De 
1 CONC esta casa pretende Atanasio de Salcedo, por hermano: todos tres pobres: de esta casa no se prover a otro". This information indicates that Alvaro de Zamora had one son and two daughters. The son was Pedro Pérez de Zamora whose bro
1 CONC ther-in-law (cuñado) was Luis de Vargas. Apparently, Luis de Vargas was married to one of Pedro's sisters and Atanasio de Salcedo was married to the second. All three were considered poor.
1 CONT
1 CONT Furthermore, Dorantes de Carranza gave this information about the father of Alvaro Pérez de Zamora:
1 CONT
1 CONT 14. Casa de Alonso Pérez de Zamora, vecino y conquistador de México.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jorge González......hijo
1 CONT
1 CONT Luis de Zamora......hijo
1 CONT
1 CONT Alvaro de Zamora.....hijo
1 CONT
1 CONT Andrés Pérez Meléndez, por la mujer....nieto
1 CONT
1 CONT Legitimos
1 CONT
1 CONT Researcher: José Antonio Esquibel
1 CONT
1 CONT Source: Batlasar Dorantes de Carranza, Sumária relación de la cosas de la Nueva España, Editorial Porrua, S.A., México, 1987, 145, 265 & 374.
1 CONT AKA: PEDRO PéREZ DE ZAMORA.
